From af43072bc95ba6a5fde0f624ecd50abbb57d57f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 21:28:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] techpack, qcacld: drop -Werror from the vendor Kbuilds

These trees are built by LineageOS with the Android prebuilt clang, which
does not diagnose what GCC 15 does. Building them with OpenEmbedded's
aarch64 cross toolchain turns a large number of pre-existing warnings -
almost all of them -Wpointer-sign in the QTI audio techpack - into hard
errors, and the build stops in techpack/audio before it reaches vmlinux.

Only vendor code is touched (techpack/, drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0,
qca-wifi-host-cmn, fw-api): -Werror is removed where it is set
unconditionally, and -Werror=<specific> forms are left alone. The warnings
themselves are unchanged and still printed.

Same treatment as the MT6739 (mindphone) port, which needed -Werror dropped
from 30 MediaTek vendor Makefiles for the same reason.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor tree is built with Android's clang]
